<section class=3D"section main-article-chapter" data-menu-title=3D"Defendin=
g against API attacks">
 <h2 class=3D"section-title"><i class=3D"icon" data-icon=3D"1"></i>Defendin=
g against API attacks</h2>
 <p>Organizations should <a href=3D"https://www.techtarget.com/searchsecuri=
ty/tip/How-to-fix-the-top-API-vulnerabilities">defend APIs</a> as they prot=
ect any traditional web application -- by following application security be=
st practices and deploying appropriate cybersecurity measures. Consider the=
 following ways to mitigate API vulnerabilities:</p>
 <ul class=3D"default-list">=20
  <li>Sanitize all query parameters that the API can interpret to prevent X=
SS, SQL injection and other similar attacks.</li>=20
  <li>Institute strong user authentication and authorization mechanisms to =
help prevent a malicious user from accessing data through an API.</li>=20
  <li>Ensure DoS and <a href=3D"https://www.techtarget.com/searchnetworking=
/answer/3-approaches-for-how-to-prevent-DDoS-attacks-on-networks">DDoS secu=
rity software</a> protects not only the main website, but APIs as well.</li=
>=20
  <li>Keep an accurate inventory of APIs exposed to the internet, and know =
which third-party organizations and users have access. Assess what type of =
and how much information the API returns to the end user, and ensure it's n=
o more than necessary.</li>=20
 </ul>
 <p><i>Rob Shapland is an ethical hacker specializing in cloud security, so=
cial engineering and delivering cybersecurity training to companies worldwi=
de.</i></p>
</section></section>






